sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-034-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) Ch. XV: eggs as solids of revolution of a definite, species-varying family of ovoid meridian curves (Preston 1953 family on Biggins et al. 2018 / Deeming 2018 data) — MorphoEval overall 90.1/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `thompson/claims/t1917-034_on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-certain-other-hollo.py` (overall weighted score: 90.1/100, up from 56.1/100 in v1). The remediated script verifies the 13 pinned dataset files at runtime, inverts Thompson's envelope equation on every egg as the excess-pressure profile (P - p_n)/T = 2H(x), closes the Preston family from four curvature constraints (C126 recovered to 5.6e-16; sphere from uniform pressure), and drives a sphere -> ovoid -> conical pressure path. It segments 12 eggs of Thompson's owl, grebe, plover and guillemot classes from five photographs (axisymmetry residual 0.4 % on the back-lit C126 silhouette, museum median 4.2 %), re-fits the C126 photograph to c = (0.488, -0.245, 0.043, 0.117) vs published (0.488, -0.246, 0.039, 0.121) (E 1.8616 vs 1.8607, profile r = 0.99999), and shows Steiner's Cartesian oval 7.4x and the ellipsoid null 31x worse than Preston on the guillemot (Thompson's own footnote). Species signal: eta^2 = 0.67 / 0.83 / 0.47 for elongation / pointedness / polar asymmetry (p < 1e-92), order-level eta^2 0.38 / 0.57 (Deeming PC1 / PC2), KS D = 0.96; prolate-never-oblate holds (min E = 1.035 over 1411 eggs); asymmetry rises with relative egg mass (rho = 0.39, p = 7e-8). Verdict written to result.json: supported, with two flagged details (King Penguin is not spherical; Thompson's pole-tension remark has the sign reversed under his own equation). Overall 90.1/100 (faithfulness 89.7, reproducibility 91.0); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 2514d4650; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scikit-image 0.26.0, lean 4.35.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 90, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_034_on_the_shapes_of_eggs_and_of_c_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-034_on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-certain-other-hollo.py at 2514d4650, image/png, 974275 B, 1694×1346 px, artifact_sha256 d8c69f3b02b18347a9c1857f851870aae7a50461ddd8c46d17f544b9ffe5afc4 (sha256 d8c69f3b02b18347a9c1857f851870aae7a50461ddd8c46d17f544b9ffe5afc4), spec_fingerprint 16220681983e59a7518d8fd164735cf554e4313c23baed4858dbc080073234a4. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 16220681983e59a7518d8fd164735cf554e4313c23baed4858dbc080073234a4; artifact_sha256: d8c69f3b02b18347a9c1857f851870aae7a50461ddd8c46d17f544b9ffe5afc4; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/biggins2018_C126_uria_aalge_silhouette.jpg=0a5c73b782104608..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/biggins2018_comparison_of_fits.csv=b2712450e2f2132e..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/biggins2018_data_for_comparing_indices.csv=39a776b94bad894a..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/biggins2018_range_of_egg_shapes.csv=3d0617dfd8cd0c20..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/deeming2018_jab_egg_shape_composition.csv=6367ba5252e52fcd..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/mwnh_0308_vanellus_vanellus_eggs.jpg=426b26bbad6c67d2..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/mwnh_0481_uria_aalge_eggs.jpg=fcaadba0ae209c4c..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/mwnh_0646_strix_aluco_egg.jpg=139f2249abb44e77..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/mwnh_1921_podiceps_cristatus_eggs.jpg=866eb96ea90025cc..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/paper_citations.bib=45e263a3bef66328..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/scout_manifest.json=83406c03aa7136ec..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-034/t1917_034_on_the_shapes_of_eggs_and_of_c_reference.json=27f65f272430a55c...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-28-t1917-034-on-the-shapes-of-eggs-and-of-c-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson 1917 p. 652: eggs are simple solids of revolution; forms range from spherical (owl, penguin, tortoise) through ellipsoidal (grebe, cormorant, pelican) and ovoid (hen) to blunt-pointed conical (guillemot, puffin, sandpiper, plover, curlew); prolate never oblate. | Thompson 1917 p. 654 footnote: Steiner's Cartesian oval r + m r' = c 'fails in such a case as the guillemot'. | Thompson 1917 p. 655 (5): the most unsymmetrical / tapered eggs are large relative to the parent bird (apteryx the exception, p. 656). | Thompson 1917 pp. 657-659: cone-ended-cylinder balance p cos^2(theta) = p' cos^2(theta'); envelope equation p_n + T(1/r + 1/r') = P; spherical egg <=> uniform p_n.; reconstructed_in_script: Preston (1953) four-parameter meridian family with Biggins et al. (2018) indices, closed-form polar asymmetry R_pole = p(+/-1)^2 and exact volume functional (Lean Laws 1-2). | Thompson closure: pole / equator curvature constraints + equator position determine the Preston coefficients; mean-curvature (excess pressure) profile of every egg; pressure-asymmetry path sphere -> ellipsoid -> conical. | Computer-vision segmentation and Preston weighted least squares (Biggins Analysis.R estimator) on 12 eggs in 5 photographs; axisymmetry residual; Cartesian-oval and ellipsoid controls. | eta^2 / Kruskal-Wallis across 30 species and 15 orders, KS test, RMSE / breadth, Spearman asymmetry vs relative egg mass.; transfer_boundary: The Preston family is a 1953 descriptor adopted as the quantitative reading of Thompson's 'definite family'; Thompson gave no algebraic family. | Biggins et al. (2018) eggs are auks and penguins (plus a 10-egg range set); order-level breadth comes only from Deeming's outline PCs; museum photographs are oblique-lit and bound the axisymmetry test from above. | The Thompson closure is a kinematic reading of his equilibrium equation (curvature <-> excess pressure), not a dynamic oviduct simulation; friction and tangential forces he mentions are not modelled.; does_not_claim: That oviduct pressure is demonstrated to be the cause of the family; only the geometric claim and the internal consistency of Thompson's equation are tested. | Anything about eggshell microstructure, colour, or non-avian hard-shelled eggs beyond Thompson's mention.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Photograph or source back-lit silhouettes of owl, grebe and plover eggs so polar asymmetry and axisymmetry are measured under the same controlled conditions as C126.",
            "remediation needed: Replace the kinematic Thompson closure with a dynamic axisymmetric membrane in a peristaltic tube (wall friction + tangential tension gradient, Thompson pp. 657-659) so that the pressure-asymmetry path is solved rather than regressed." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.901"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 228 Pass 2 Assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

